{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues","id":1073595,"title":"[2E] First Change Story issues","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-04T23:20:32-07:00","id":1073595,"title":"[2E] First Change Story issues","content":"I start new <b>Werewolf </b>chronicle and want to run Prelude story for my players, as all would be noobs in <b>Forsaken</b>. From time I got 2E corebook, I wanted to run \u2018First Change teenagers\u2019 story, from page 291 of book. More, most players are interested in \u2018childhood friends\u2019 group concept, so I think that this \u2018Stand By Me-like\u2019 story would be great. BUT the proper chronicle will be with full proper Pack and \u2018grown up\u2019 Uratha characters, after Tribe Initiation ( needs of setting and Open Table here ). So I think I will need at least 5 years downtime ( if First Change will be in senior year of High School for characters ), as I want them to be able to \u2018grow up\u2019 on their own, at least a bit.<br /> <br /> <b>Problem I have is how to run it then?</b> First Change Story scenario assumes that characters are like Pack just after end of it. More, fresh <b>WtF</b> 2E character after creation is assumed to end just Tribe Initiation \u2013 it can be few months after Change, but I hardly see possible to stretch it as to 5 years downtime between First Change and start of proper chronicle. Any ideas how to solve this? And no, running only few months after Change will not solve it, as players want to have some freedom to lead character history after Prelude story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T01:45:36-07:00","id":1073623,"title":"","content":"older uratha and/or spirit mentor figure guides them into being a full pack, duh... Best part is, when the pack are grown up, the mentor can come back to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X8pWjiFxXkg\" target=\"_blank\">save </a>the pack at a critical moment and then get <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LjFWH7GuXb4\" target=\"_blank\">killed </a>for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hh-zGP-LcQQ\" target=\"_blank\">drama</a>/<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sq51w34Hg9I\" target=\"_blank\">motivation. </a><br /> <br /> <br /> Because that is how these things are done.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T02:01:05-07:00","id":1073626,"title":"","content":"Just start the chronicle without the full Gifts, Renown, Merits and such &quot;standard&quot; starting characters are supposed to get. A fair tradeoff for the roleplaying experience, I'd say.<br /> <br /> And of course you the Storyteller can be generous with Beats on earlier parts of the chronicle, should you feel the player characters are too inexperienced to hang with 'proper' Uratha. After all, the main characters hog the spotlight <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T03:01:55-07:00","id":1073646,"title":"","content":"I don't think tribal initiation takes quite that long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T03:17:46-07:00","id":1073648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1073646#post1073646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think tribal initiation takes quite that long.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can take as little as a week, or as much as a year.<br /> <br /> The issue with first changees is that their harmony will start pretty high, and those are some pretty horrific times for the characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-05T03:46:40-07:00","id":1073655,"title":"","content":"<b>I don't have problem with <i>'young Uratha will have too much Gifts or Renowns just after First Change story'</i>, as I literally want to cut it short day, maybe two after the Change itself, when new werewolves are spligting. </b>Beside wild activated Forms, they will probably do not have ANYTHING from Werewolf Character Template just after Change. See scenario on page 291, that I want to run - it's this with mortal character having Tension risen as to what moment the Change commerce ( or don't, and character is only Wolf-Blooded then ). I even think about making players choose only some Skills they teenage PCs would have, declared in the moment of first use - like on <i>The Funeral</i> or <i>First Hunt</i> ( from <b>The Pack</b> book ) scenarios.<br /> <br /> <b>What I have problem with is that I need PCs from First Change story to have few years of break</b>, to let PC them grow in other directions after game. Five years would be A LOT in Uratha life and like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> pointed - Tribe Initiation only takes as much as year. That means PCs will have like 4 years on their own, beside coming together once more at start on proper chronicle start. <b>That sound a much more tough ( or experienced ) characters than those from Werewolf Creation rules. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> Maybe I'm overthinking it too much here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T02:15:17-07:00","id":1074061,"title":"","content":"Other problem with First Change Story scenario - <b>If characters get Integrity Breaking Point in times of running scenario - Should she roll it? </b>After transformation into Uratha she will have Harmony on 9, either way, and Wolf-Blooded <i>end</i> with Breaking Point on Integrity and getting second Tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T03:34:21-07:00","id":1074074,"title":"","content":"Hm. Why do you need them to be adults? Can you not just roll with them being teens and struggling to come to terms and support each other? Then as been suggested an older werewolf finds them and brings them to be initiated. <br /> <br /> By then once they settle and find a tribe you could probably do a time skip and the players aren't missing out on crucial rp development. Each character is taken by their chosen tribe to train and learn, so a few years later they meet up again maybe because of a promise to come back together to start their own pack.<br /> <br /> I'd roll for breaking points for this because it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T04:16:28-07:00","id":1074086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074074#post1074074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. Why do you need them to be adults? Can you not just roll with them being teens and struggling to come to terms and support each other? Then as been suggested an older werewolf finds them and brings them to be initiated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beacuse my first PCs group will be only (main) but part of Pack - rest of players will come and go but they all be connected by Pack as EXTENDED organisation. Like, ' few dozen cultists of ancient spirit' not 'me and my two buddies'. Also, I would rather give PCs time to 'go their own way' - like one player is interested in playing cops, other with priest, and one to be ganger. One year in late teens ( 19+ year old ) does not seems as being possible to become character like that. MAYBE 3 years, but more like 5 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:17:03-07:00","id":1074211,"title":"","content":"Ok so why not have their first change as adults instead of teens?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T10:35:57-07:00","id":1074224,"title":"","content":"Ok, so to re-phrase the problem a little bit, you are planning to run an introductory First Change story as sort of a prelude to the main Chronicle, which will take place after a 5 year timeskip, featuring the same characters, now grown up and part of a pack together. But, you are concerned because the characters would most likely be ready for Tribal Initiation shortly after the end of the First Change prelude, but you want the post-timeskip chronicle to start them off shortly after Tribal Initiation, and a five-year Initiation seems like a stretch. Is that about right?<br /> <br /> How important is it to you that the post-timeskip Chronicle be right after Initiation? Could you instead start them off with some extra Experience (maybe multiply the experience earned in the pre-timeskip prelude by 5 or something) and say that by the start of the post-timeskip Chronicle they're all experienced hunters that may have spent some time as lone wolves, or joined and later left another pack or packs, before meeting back up with their old high school friends and deciding to form a pack with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:07:36-07:00","id":1074285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074211#post1074211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok so why not have their first change as adults instead of teens?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>First Change Story</i> advised to run it as teens. Also, wanted to add this 'hormonal battles' feel to it and teenage angst. And half of players will be my previous <b>Mage</b> players - with running on adults First Change, it will be look more or like 'Awakening for werewolves' to them, probably. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I really wanted to run this Prelude story to mark different feel of <b>Werewolf</b> to <b>Mage</b> for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:16:10-07:00","id":1074290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074224#post1074224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so to re-phrase the problem a little bit, you are planning to run an introductory First Change story as sort of a prelude to the main Chronicle, which will take place after a 5 year timeskip, featuring the same characters, now grown up and part of a pack together. But, you are concerned because the characters would most likely be ready for Tribal Initiation shortly after the end of the First Change prelude, but you want the post-timeskip chronicle to start them off shortly after Tribal Initiation, and a five-year Initiation seems like a stretch. Is that about right?</div> </div> </div> </div>General idea is right - I want to run Prelude in 'home town' of teenage characters. Then run timeskip five years to let them 'grown up' in different lives. Problem is that they will be werewolves for five years before proper chronicle start then. So they will need higher stats. maybe?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074224#post1074224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How important is it to you that the post-timeskip Chronicle be right after Initiation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I plan to run timeskip <i>right after First Change</i>, even. Change will shatter their lives, they will need to rebuild them into &lt;their each PCs ending concept&gt;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074224#post1074224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you instead start them off with some extra Experience (maybe multiply the experience earned in the pre-timeskip prelude by 5 or something) and say that by the start of the post-timeskip Chronicle they're all experienced hunters that may have spent some time as lone wolves, or joined and later left another pack or packs, before meeting back up with their old high school friends and deciding to form a pack with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, probably will run with extra XP. I see a problem as (main) PCs group will be starting point of proper Pack, they will get extra XP on begining of chronicle - and players that will join later will not have. But those next player will join after starts so it will be somehow fair they will have only chargen PCs?<br /> <br /> And earned Beats in Prelude * 5 sounds good for extra start XP for (main) PCs, I think on beginning of proper chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-06-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T13:31:19-07:00","id":1074298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074290#post1074290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, probably will run with extra XP. I see a problem as (main) PCs group will be starting point of proper Pack, they will get extra XP on begining of chronicle - and players that will join later will not have. But those next player will join after starts so it will be somehow fair they will have only chargen PCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it depends on how you and your players feel about PCs with different exp levels. If you're the sort who prefers to use group Beats and Experiences, or if your players are used to playing in games where everyone in the group stays at the same exp level, I would not recommend starting players who join after the prelude with less exp than the ones who did do the prelude. Either start them off with the same exp as the rest of the party, or run them through a solo mini-prelude to get them up to speed with the rest of the group. If you're like me and have no problem with some PCs having more exp than others, and if your players are ok with that, then sure, start people who join later at base character creation. LARPers and former LARPers will probably have an easier time accepting this style of play than people who are more familiar with tabletop, as will old-school grognards tend to be more comfortable with it than current-gen gamers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T15:28:30-07:00","id":1074351,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just track the total XP that was gained past chargen and you are good to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-06T23:20:48-07:00","id":1074532,"title":"","content":"Problem is that this game is made as closest to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006024-open-table-model-with-cod-games\">Open Table model</a> as I can with <b>Werewolf</b> game. I want it to be simple chargen and probably even Group Beats ( first time I think about this kind mechanics ) for new players. I also assume that PCs that go with Prelude will probably be main players, with rest going 'on and off', probably. Maybe I will go with simple chargen, but let rest join with 'stored' XP like Prelude lowest characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-07T03:34:05-07:00","id":1074573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1074532#post1074532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is that this game is made as closest to <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1006024-open-table-model-with-cod-games&amp;quot;]Open</a> Table model[/URL] as I can with <b>Werewolf</b> game. I want it to be simple chargen and probably even Group Beats ( first time I think about this kind mechanics ) for new players. I also assume that PCs that go with Prelude will probably be main players, with rest going 'on and off', probably. Maybe I will go with simple chargen, but let rest join with 'stored' XP like Prelude lowest characters?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't implement an open table format &amp; group beats without being grossly unfair to the non recurrent characters, or to the recurrent PCs in the event of non-recurrent gaining access to the xp pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T01:44:45-07:00","id":1075404,"title":"","content":"I found other problem with First Change Story scenario - as each character has rising Tension pool, and suddenly it can burst - <b>What about then character miss her pointed Auspice?</b> Like in story we have Full Moon, Tension is enough high, but player wanted his character to be Elodoth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T10:22:36-07:00","id":1075517,"title":"","content":"Don't schedule your story on an actual Lunar calendar. When they change, it just happens to be the phase they wanted to change in.<br /> <br /> Or if you really want them to play a regimented story, what they want as their auspice doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2017, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:08:02-07:00","id":1075672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1075404#post1075404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found other problem with First Change Story scenario - as each character has rising Tension pool, and suddenly it can burst - <b>What about then character miss her pointed Auspice?</b> Like in story we have Full Moon, Tension is enough high, but player wanted his character to be Elodoth?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sneaky way to go about it: it's a lunar eclipse. Person wants to be an Elodath? They change the moment the moon's shadow is half. Boom. It's tricky, and you can always flavor it that the character runs a little more aggressive than most Elodath, but it's there if you want to actually fit a lunar calander into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T19:35:47-07:00","id":1075680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1073595-2e-first-change-story-issues?p=1075672#post1075672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sneaky way to go about it: it's a lunar eclipse. Person wants to be an Elodoth? They change the moment the moon's shadow is half. Boom. It's tricky, and you can always flavor it that the character runs a little more aggressive than most Elodath, but it's there if you want to actually fit a lunar calander into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I like it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But what about other way around? Only one player I have decided on Auspice and that's Rahu. <b>How to 'pack' Full Moon on real phases of Half Moon, Gibbous Moon or Crescent Moon?</b> I suspect that in time of No Moon is out of question any other Auspice to have.<br /> <br /> Rest of my players are more or less too fresh for <b>Werewolf</b> and probably be mostly okay from game events Auspices for characters ( if even going for whole Uratha in the first place, in scenario they can end as Wolf-Blooded if they want to ). <b>So I should aim for story finale in Full Moon, with having one sure Rahu?</b><br /> <br /> But what about considering Tension? If we take preRahu character, he probably will have rather high Tension ( low Willpower, have Nighmares as Conditon from start ), so he can hit easily First Change in any nearest Tension infusing situation. <b>As I wanted to run with this story game about Swedish Prom night in high school ( and few days earlier or later ) should I start story on day-two before Prom?</b> Especially, as it is Full Moon then?<br /> <br /> And last but not least question on First Change. Tension rise with stressful interactions of teenagers. Most of those are made in day. But First Change is <i>always</i> under the Moon. So what - <b>If Tension rise, First Changer loose character for the rest of the day, waits whole hours and player cannot do anything with him after he is found next morning, totally naked or someones guts on his hands? </b>Tension is constructed that way it probably hit rather in day time, than night time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2017, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:34:03-07:00","id":1078475,"title":"","content":"I today sorta solved problem with wrong Moon Phase to the working Auspice player is aiming - In Shadow Realm, Luna can make anything with sky, yes? So when our pre-Ithaeur was hitting Tension in Full Moon DAY, we run she heard spirits voice, partially changed shifted between Flesh and Shadow Realm - and when she entered then, <b>in <i>whole</i> local Shadow Realm was Crescent Moon on sky</b> ( even if there was day in Flesh then ) - cause Luna wanted it to be, right now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-02T02:01:17-08:00","id":1172577,"title":"","content":"For all those months I run few more First Changes in time of our normal play, outside scenarios 'we all are teenagers' model - I found that normal Tension Pool starting number can be to high for new players joining running chronicle and NOT Change in one or two game sessions - dice rolled are simply too high and even two rolls per character in game session ends in Change. <br /> <br /> On next player joining our game I will start with HALF of Tension that WtF 2E corebook advise, to let player accustom to being Wolf-Blooded first. I will write in few weeks how it went for this PC and player on rising Change in WB then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T19:33:01-08:00","id":1281610,"title":"","content":"Few weeks became one year, but using HALF of starting Tension Pools seems to work for giving player a 2-3 games sessions of play on character. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> As to other subtopics - the 'No proper Moon for Auspice' problem is somehow solved by natural phenomena. Today, when returning from work, I saw a Gibbous Moon on the sky <i>in the mid day</i>!<b> So if at least general Auspice time is good, First Change can even be in the day</b>, only sun need to be somehow not direct then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}